B = [
('Riva','Europe','1950s-70s','boats',"In the style of Riva, glamorous Italian mid-century luxury expressed in finish and material. Deep red-brown mahogany veneer polished to a mirror gloss, with caramel and honey striped wood inlay laid in long parallel bands. Bright polished chrome trim, slim white or cream painted lines and padded leather in cream, white and fiery red, lifted by sudden aqua turquoise accents. Smooth, long, tapering, streamlined silhouettes with soft rounded ends and sleek curved edges. Small enamel flag-colour details in green, white and red, a refined upright emblem and flowing, slim italic script lettering in white or gold. Handmade, sensual, sleek, sunlit and richly refined."),
('Chris-Craft','North America','1930s-50s','boats',"In the style of Chris-Craft, classic varnished American craftsmanship. Warm honey to red-brown mahogany planking with fine pale seams, polished to a deep glassy shine. Chrome and brass trim, tufted leather in red and cream, and small enamel badge discs in orange, black and cream with bold stripes. Rounded, streamlined, softly flared forms with slim tapering lines. Lettering is a joined, flowing cursive script with a long swash underline, cast in polished metal or printed in black and red on cream signboards, paired with tidy condensed capitals. Vintage red, navy, cream and chrome palette, handcrafted, nostalgic, sporty and carefree."),
('Meccano','Europe','1900s-60s','toys',"In the style of Meccano, an technical-manual look built from printed panels in strong red, deep green, cream and mustard yellow. Bold slab and block capitals with heavy outline and drop shadow, set inside framed banner panels, often with a big stylised letter M in a contrasting square. Fine ruled borders, numbered labels, line-engraved diagrams in black ink on aged cream paper and tidy rows of evenly spaced round perforations. Metal surfaces in red enamel, green enamel, bright zinc and polished brass, joined by small hex bolts. Edwardian, orderly, industrious, tactile and nostalgic."),
('Hornby','Europe','1920s-60s','toys',"In the style of Hornby, nostalgic British tinplate toy-maker design. Flat printed metal and card panels in tomato red, teal green, cream and deep blue with fine gold lining, tiny printed rivets and painted tile and masonry patterns. Lettering is a bold, outlined, slightly arched capital face and a delicate flowing script with a tidy underline, often within a rectangular panel with a ruled border. Glossy lacquer, polished brass details and slight enamel crazing give honest age. Sleek streamlined emblem graphics with speed lines and a rounded wing shape. Orderly, charming, mid-century catalogue style with a cheerful, collectable feel."),
('Matchbox','Europe','1950s-60s','toys',"In the style of Matchbox, small collectable British die-cast character. Saturated primary yellow panels with blue and red end sections, bordered by fine black and white lines. A bold arched title in red capitals with a white outline sits over a banner reading in simple block letters, with a tidy numbered corner label and a small black and white crest. Painted metal in subdued period colours of pastel green, powder blue, terracotta red, cream and silver, with soft cast detail and tiny silver highlights. Modest, practical, everyday, tidy and nostalgic, with slightly worn printed card and thin paper texture."),
('Steiff','Europe','1900s-present','toys',"In the style of Steiff, soft heirloom German craft. Mohair, felt and woven fur in honey gold, cinnamon, caramel, cream and smoky brown, with slightly worn, loved tips and fine hand-stitched seams in dark thread. Small black glass-bead eyes, stitched noses and softly rounded, slightly humped, long-limbed proportions. A signature small metal stud with a tiny flag-like yellow tag carrying red script lettering and a little elephant emblem. Printed labels use cream, red and gold with elegant script and sturdy serif capitals. Antique, tender, sentimental, tactile and carefully made, with a warm nursery calm."),
('Ravensburger','Europe','1950s-present','toys',"In the style of Ravensburger, sturdy German family-product design. A deep royal blue banner and a navy and white wordmark in a clean, slightly rounded, wide-spaced sans-serif, with a small blue triangle emblem. Layouts have crisp white borders, tidy information panels and glossy printed cardboard surfaces, with a glossy, richly saturated painted illustration style full of warm colour, soft gradients, fine detail and storybook fantasy motifs. Secondary accents in bright orange, green, yellow and sky blue. Trustworthy, orderly, cheerful, high-quality and European, with a polished, slightly nostalgic finish and generous clean margins around every printed block of colour."),
('Opel','Europe','1930s-70s','cars',"In the style of Opel, neat, sporty, mass-market German design. A zigzag lightning bolt emblem inside a ring, and a long thin bolt stroke set beside bold wide capital lettering in white, black or silver on a diagonal panel. Compact, tidy, sharply creased forms with narrow chrome edges and neat rectangular badges. Palette of signal yellow, bright orange, lime green, sky blue, white and black, plus period greys and enamel red. Lettering is chunky, slanted, italic block capitals. Clean ring-and-bolt geometry, dynamic diagonals, crisp and youthful, with a pragmatic, friendly, quietly sporty character."),
('Austin','Europe','1920s-60s','cars',"In the style of Austin, rounded, sensible and homely British motoring heritage. Stately soft curves, tall upright proportions and narrow chrome edging. Winged, pointed-star style emblems in polished chrome and enamel, with elegant script and spaced serif capitals. Paint in black, maroon, deep green, grey, cream, sky blue and pastel red, often in two-tone panels with a fine contrasting line. Printed literature uses flat gouache-style illustration, simple colour blocking, wide margins and cream paper with old-fashioned italic type. Polished wood veneer, thick leather in beige and maroon, and tidy chrome details. Modest, dependable, comfortable, wholesome and nostalgic."),
('Morgan','Europe','1930s-present','cars',"In the style of Morgan, hand-built, charming and deliberately pre-war British craft. A winged badge with a blue cross-shaped centre, silver-grey feathered wings and a bold capital name, drawn in chrome, enamel and cream. Racing green, claret, cream, navy, ivory and polished silver with brass and chrome trim. Materials are aluminium panels over ash wood, quilted leather with contrast stitching, canvas, wire and polished timber. Forms are slim, long, curved and light, with flowing separate swept shapes and rounded ends. Lettering is crisp, upright and slightly spaced. Handcrafted, nostalgic, cheerful and quietly proud."),
]
